---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy – placeholder" description="Placeholder for the privacy policy of the fictional Faserlauf workshop, with the facts about what this demo site stores. Demo project." noindex>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy policy' }]} />
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="placeholder-note">
        <strong>Placeholder.</strong> A real business needs a complete privacy policy under the GDPR, reviewed by a lawyer. The facts
        below describe what this demo site actually does, so they can be the basis of that text.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap prose section">
    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>[Name and address of the business, contact for data protection questions]</p>

    <h2>What this site stores</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No cookies, no tracking, no third-party services.</strong> Fonts and all images are served from this server; no map, video or analytics provider is embedded.</li>
      <li><strong>Your cookie choice</strong> is stored in your browser’s local storage (key <code>fl-consent-v1</code>), not sent to us.</li>
      <li><strong>Your configuration</strong> lives in the page address (URL) only. It reaches us only if you send a request.</li>
      <li><strong>Quote requests</strong> (name, email, optional phone, postcode, message, the configuration and an image of it) and <strong>contact messages</strong> are stored on this server to answer you. [Retention period, e.g. deleted after 6 months if no order follows.]</li>
      <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> [What the hosting provider logs, e.g. IP address for 7 days for security.]</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Legal basis</h2>
    <p>[Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR for steps prior to a contract at your request; Art. 6(1)(f) for server logs.]</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>[Access, rectification, erasure, restriction, data portability, objection, complaint to the Berlin Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information.]</p>

    <h2>Statistics</h2>
    <p>
      The cookie notice offers “Allow statistics”. On this demo site no statistics tool is installed; the choice only exists so a
      privacy-friendly tool can be added later without changing the notice.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .placeholder-note {
    background: var(--warn-soft);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--paper-2);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
